# oracle: native binary restart (serial file, b332f28 write_restart) of atomic lj/cut with 2 types, a mixed (unset) pair and pair_modify shift; the restarted run continues 100 steps
# oracle-inputs: w184nr_lj.restart
# native: b332f28 built as the parity binary wrote w184nr_lj.restart (100 steps of fcc velocity-create lj melt, 2 types)
read_restart    w184nr_lj.restart
neighbor        0.3 bin
thermo_style    custom step temp epair emol etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
fix             1 all nve
run             100
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12
# measured: max relative error 6.6e-13 (fz of atom 60 after 100 steps; thermo rows agree to 1 ulp), so the tolerance is 1e-9
